From 028623069a5bcacd51b2df3b3aa483c0f93b2957 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 04:55:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Public RPC host role: a browser profile's RPC origin
 answered by the operator's own Base node

network/public-rpc.mjs (+ public-rpc-config.mjs, kept free of a main check so the
runner and privacy-agent bundles carry the validator only): role 'public-rpc'
- exact method allowlist from the browser note, EIP-1898 block objects, reverts
  passed through (code/reason/data); admin/debug/personal/signing/txpool/filters,
  batches, oversized bodies, other paths/verbs refused without reaching the node
- node = loopback only (the operator's own client/holder); optional loopback
  chainVerifier answers only its proven methods, never falls back; every answer
  names its source (X-Enclave-Rpc-Source) and host (X-Enclave-Rpc-Host)
- syncing/stale/unreachable node -> 503; stall -> 504 at the deadline; body,
  response, in-flight, rate and log-range bounds; CORS for configured origins
- eth_sendRawTransaction refused unless the operator states a propagation route
- not indexed (kind null): runner refuses publicEndpoints, never advertised;
  hostId must be keccak(host.endpoint)

Opt-in naming/ingress: rpc-<b32>.<zone> (host-service-names), requested by a host
serving the role (service request rpc:true) and granted only by exits that opted
in (hostServices.rpc); refused by name otherwise; all other grants unchanged.
stage-tool publishes the label; browser-profile --verify-chain refuses two RPCs
of one host (public-rpc-hosts.mjs).

Tests: public-rpc (reth v2.8.0 --dev), public-rpc-browser (Chromium, packaged
roles), lifecycle opt-in cases, verifier-roles ban/unban/owner migration with the
packaged role.
